  "transcript": "A product feels disposable when fixing it becomes harder than replacing it. Sometimes the part is not available. Sometimes the tool is special. Sometimes the repair costs almost as much as buying a new one. And sometimes the product looks at you and says, \"You own me, but not enough to open me.\" Very healthy relationship. This is why repairability matters. Repairability just means how easy something is to fix. That is basically society looking at a phone and saying, please have a future.",
